# gborges Wi-Fi seed configuration.
#
# Copy this file to wifi.conf (sibling of this one, .gitignored) and edit.
# At build time, common.mk installs wifi.conf to /system/etc/gborges/wifi.conf
# IF it exists in the source tree. On first boot the gborges-wifi-seed
# init service reads it and runs `cmd wifi add-network` for each entry,
# adding them to the saved-networks list so Android auto-joins whichever
# is in range.
#
# Sourced by /system/bin/gborges-wifi-seed (POSIX sh). Quote values; no
# command substitution.
#
# Format: numbered variables. Networks are read sequentially starting at
# index 1 — the loop stops at the first missing SSID_N (no gaps).
#
# Per-network keys (N = 1, 2, 3, ...):
#
#   SSID_N        required, quoted string
#   PSK_N         required for SECURITY_N=wpa2 / wpa3, quoted string
#   SECURITY_N    optional: open | wpa2 (default) | wpa3
#   HIDDEN_N      optional: 0 (default) | 1
#
# Examples:
#
#   SSID_1="HomeNet"
#   PSK_1="correct horse battery staple"
#   SECURITY_1=wpa2
#
#   SSID_2="OfficeNet"
#   PSK_2="hunter2"
#   SECURITY_2=wpa3
#
#   SSID_3="OpenGuestAP"
#   SECURITY_3=open
#
# Reseeding: the script writes /data/local/tmp/.gborges-wifi-seeded as a
# one-shot marker. Factory-reset wipes /data and re-seeds; otherwise
# delete the marker and reboot.
